      "storyTitle": "From the hills to your home",
      "storySub": "",
      "storySteps": [
        {
          "title": "It begins at 14,000 ft",
          "text": "In Mustang, Chyangra goats grow a soft undercoat against the Himalayan winter. Each spring it is combed out by hand.",
          "image": "https://images.pexels.com/photos/11733651/pexels-photo-11733651.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200"
        },
        {
          "title": "Spun and woven by hand",
          "text": "Weavers in Palpa and Kathmandu spin the fibre and work it on wooden looms, one pattern at a time.",
          "image": "https://images.pexels.com/photos/6634555/pexels-photo-6634555.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200"
        },
        {
          "title": "Checked and wrapped",
          "text": "Every piece gets a Craft Passport with its maker, place and technique, then is wrapped in lokta paper.",
          "image": "https://images.pexels.com/photos/18681553/pexels-photo-18681553.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200"
        },
        {
          "title": "Delivered to your door",
          "text": "Your money is held until it arrives safely, then paid straight to the artisan.",
          "image": "https://images.pexels.com/photos/11404647/pexels-photo-11404647.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1200"
        }
      ],
